+The filtering can be written with the `filter()` function from the
+`r BiocStyle::Biocpkg("tidySummarizedExperiment")` package, which brings the
+tidyverse syntax to `SummarizedExperiment` objects, including `TreeSE`
+(see also the tidy R programming section in [@sec-datawrangling]). Here we keep
+the features with a standard deviation above zero.
+
 ```{r}
 #| label: filter_sd
 
-selected <- rowData(tse)[["sd"]] > 0
-tse_sub <- tse[selected, ]
+library(tidySummarizedExperiment)
+
+tse_sub <- tse |> filter(sd > 0)
 tse_sub
 ```
 
